-- title:
--   Lifting q-torsion points and Drinfeld partners to base change
-- statement:
--   **Numerical and moduli data over $A_0$.** Fix a prime $q$, a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, a nonzero natural number $M'$, and a commutative ring $A_0$. Two stability hypotheses are imposed over all $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ` states that for every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every quadruple $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ of [`ModularCurve.LevelPData`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L43), the predicate [`ModularCurve.IsLevelPStructure W ℓ D`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L104) (both pairs satisfy the affine equation of $W$, both $x$-coordinates are roots of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, and the two independence elements $\mathrm{indepElt}\,W\,\ell\,x_P\,x_Q$ and $\mathrm{indepElt}\,W\,\ell\,x_Q\,x_P$ are units) is inherited by $C\bullet W$ with $D$ transformed by $C$; `hM` states that the predicate [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt W p k h`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) — which for $p^k=2$ is `W.IsTwoKernel h` and otherwise is `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` (degree at most $\varphi(p^k)/2$, coefficient $1$ in that degree, $h\cdot W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}}\mid W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and $h$ dividing the relevant multiplication numerators) — is inherited by $C\bullet W$ with $h$ transformed by [`ModularCurve.kernelVariableChangeDeg`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassLevelComponents.html#L104). Further, $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: a points-evaluation exists) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the identity section is cut out by an origin chart with $x/y=z/y=0$); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q` of raw Drinfeld pairs, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`: the transported $P$ and $Q$ pull back to the original ones along `Proj.map` of any variable-change, resp. coefficient, homomorphism). Finally $P_0$ is an absolute level moduli package over $A_0$ for the level moduli datum of `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, i.e. of the rigid Weierstrass data obtained from the product of the $\Gamma_0$ prime-power component for $M'$, the level-$\ell$ component, and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component attached to $(\mathcal G,\mathcal T)$: a ring $P_0.B_0$ with an $A_0$-algebra structure and a universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ such that every point of the datum over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $P_0.B_0\to T$.
--
--   **Deformation frame.** $R$ is a noetherian local $A_0$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with $\iota : P_0.B_0\to_{A_0} R$; $k$ is a field of characteristic $q$ in which $\ell$ and $M'$ are nonzero; $\mathrm{res}_R : R\to k$ is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal of $R$. $W_0$ is a complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$ and residue map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0\to k$ surjective with kernel the maximal ideal, and $A_0\to W_0\to R$ is a scalar tower with $\mathrm{res}_R\circ\mathrm{algebraMap}_{W_0R}=\mathrm{res}_0$. The hypothesis `hfac` is the universal property of $(R,\iota)$: for every Artinian local $W_0$- and $A_0$-algebra $T$ in the tower, with residue map $\mathrm{res}_T$ onto $k$ having kernel the maximal ideal and restricting to $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$, and every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : P_0.B_0\to T$ lifting $\mathrm{res}_R\circ\iota$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\Phi : R\to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T\circ\Phi=\mathrm{res}_R$ and $\Phi\circ\iota=\varphi$.
--
--   **The étale package over $W_0$.** The hypotheses `hℓ'` and `hM'` are the variable-change stability statements above, now over all $W_0$-algebras, and `h𝒢r`, `h𝒢Or` assert that the restriction of scalars $\mathcal G|_{W_0}$ is again chord–tangent and origin-normalised. Then $P_{et}$ is an absolute level moduli package over $W_0$ for the rigid data built from the product of the $\Gamma_0$ prime-power component for $M'$, the level-$\ell$ component, and the trivial component; $x_{et}$ is a raw representative over $P_{et}.B_0$ (a Weierstrass curve $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ with unit discriminant, a family of $\Gamma_0$ generator polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, level-$\ell$ data, and a trivial slot), and `hxet` says that its class is $P_{et}.\mathrm{univ}$.
--
--   **The ring of $q$-torsion points and its deformation ring.** $CQ$ is a commutative ring which is both a $P_{et}.B_0$- and a $W_0$-algebra in a scalar tower, $Q_u$ is a point of the projective model of $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $P_{et}.B_0\to CQ$, killed by $q$-fold addition in $\mathcal G|_{W_0}$ (`hQu`), and `hrep` states that $CQ$ represents the $q$-torsion: for every $P_{et}.B_0$-algebra $T$, a $T$-point $Q$ of the model is $q$-torsion if and only if there is a unique $P_{et}.B_0$-algebra map $\chi : CQ\to T$ with $\mathrm{Spec}(\chi)$ followed by $Q_u$ equal to $Q$. Next $S$ is a noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with $\iota_S : CQ\to_{W_0} S$ and a surjection $\mathrm{res}_S : S\to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal and restricting to $\mathrm{res}_0$; `hfacS` is the corresponding universal property of $(S,\iota_S)$ against Artinian local $W_0$-algebras with residue field data over $\mathrm{res}_0$. Finally $F_S$ is a formal group over $S$ whose power series is the formal group law of the base change of $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ along $\iota_S\circ\mathrm{algebraMap}$ (`hFS`), and a Weierstrass-type factorisation of its $q$-series is given: $g\in S[X]$ is monic of degree $q-1$ with all coefficients of index $<q-1$ in the maximal ideal and constant coefficient $q$ times a unit, $v$ is a unit power series, and $F_S.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q = X\cdot g\cdot v$.
--
--   **Residual data over $k$.** With $A_0$- and $W_0$-algebra structures on $k$ in a tower, a $P_{et}.B_0$-algebra structure on $k$, and $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{W_0k}=\mathrm{res}_0$: $\rho : P_0.B_0\to_{A_0}k$ equals $\mathrm{res}_R\circ\iota$; $\psi_{et} : P_{et}.B_0\to_{W_0}k$ equals $\mathrm{res}_S\circ\iota_S\circ\mathrm{algebraMap}$ and computes the structure map $P_{et}.B_0\to k$; the discriminant of $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ base changed along $\psi_{et}$ is a unit (`hΔk`); $Q_k$ is a section of that reduced curve which is pinned to $Q_u$ in the sense that for some graded homomorphism $\varphi$ between the gradings of the two projective models, subject to the inclusion of the irrelevant ideal of the target in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source, which is a coefficient homomorphism for $\psi_{et}$ (`IsCoefficientHom`: constants $a$ go to constants $\psi_{et}(a)$ and the three coordinate classes are preserved), one has $Q_k$ followed by `Proj.map` $\varphi$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{res}_S\circ\iota_S)$ followed by $Q_u$; and $Q_k$ is not the identity section (`hQk`). The reduced level data are required to be of the right type: `hhk` gives `IsGamma0PowAt` for the reduced curve at each prime factor $p$ of $M'$ with exponent $M'.\mathrm{factorization}\,p$ and the reduced polynomial, `hDk` gives the level-$\ell$ structure for the reduced level-$\ell$ data, and `hyk` states that the raw Drinfeld pair consisting of the reduced curve, its identity section, and $Q_k$ is of level $q$, i.e. its curve is the reduced curve and for the corresponding unit discriminant the pair (identity, $Q_k$) is a Drinfeld basis in the sense that the divisor of the $q^2$ combinations coincides with the $q$-torsion ideal. Lastly `hρyk` identifies the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\rho$ with the class of this assembled raw datum over $k$.
--
--   **The test object.** $T$ is an Artinian local $W_0$-algebra with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T\to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which restricts to $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$; $\psi : P_{et}.B_0\to_{W_0}T$ satisfies $\mathrm{res}_T\circ\psi=\psi_{et}$; and $Q_m : \mathrm{Spec}\,T\to \mathrm{Proj}$ of the model of $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ lies over $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi)$ (`hQover`), is killed by $q$-fold addition in $\mathcal G|_{W_0}$ over $P_{et}.B_0$ (`hQtors`), and reduces to $Q_u$ in the sense that $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{res}_T)$ followed by $Q_m$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{res}_S\circ\iota_S)$ followed by $Q_u$ (`hQred`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $W_T$ for the base change $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ along $\psi$, whose discriminant is a unit by base change of $x_{et}.\mathrm{isUnit}_\Delta$. Then there exists a section $Q$ of the projective model of $W_T$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,T$ such that:
--
--   (i) $q$-fold iterated addition of $Q$ in the law $(\mathcal G|_{W_0})\,T\,W_T$ over the identity base equals the identity section;
--
--   (ii) for no ring homomorphism $\chi$ from the origin chart ring of $W_T$ to $T$ does `ReducesToOrigin Q χ (maximalIdeal T)` hold, that is, $Q$ does not reduce to the origin modulo the maximal ideal of $T$;
--
--   (iii) for every graded homomorphism $\varphi$ from the grading of the model of $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ to that of $W_T$, together with the inclusion of the irrelevant ideal of the target in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source, which is a coefficient homomorphism for $\psi$, the composite of $Q$ with `Proj.map` $\varphi$ equals $Q_m$;
--
--   (iv) there is an equivalence $e$ between the set of morphisms $P_m : \mathrm{Spec}\,T\to\mathrm{Proj}$ of the model of $x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ such that both $P_m$ and $Q_m$ lie over $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi)$ and the resulting pair is a relative Drinfeld basis of level $q$ over the base morphism $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi)$ for $(\mathcal G|_{W_0})\,P_{et}.B_0\,x_{et}.\mathrm{curve}$ (equality of `basisDivisorOver` and `torsionIdealOver`), and such that $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{res}_T)$ followed by $P_m$ is the underlying morphism of the identity section over $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi_{et})$, and the set of sections $P$ of the model of $W_T$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,T$ which reduce to the origin modulo the maximal ideal of $T$ for some origin chart homomorphism and for which $(P,Q)$ is a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $(\mathcal G|_{W_0})\,T\,W_T$ (equality of `basisDivisor` and `torsionIdeal`); and this equivalence is compatible with descent: for every $P_m$ in the first set and every coefficient homomorphism $\varphi$ as in (iii), the composite of the section $e(P_m)$ with `Proj.map` $\varphi$ equals $P_m$.
--
--   This is the base-change, or transport, step in the Katz–Mazur style study of Drinfeld $\Gamma(q)$-structures on the universal curve carrying $\Gamma_0(M')$ prime-power data, a level-$\ell$ structure and a $q$-torsion point: a $q$-torsion $T$-point of the universal curve over the étale package is realised as a section of the base-changed curve, not reducing to the origin, and its Drinfeld partners are matched with those partners that do reduce to the origin, compatibly with the cartesian square given by `Proj.map` of a coefficient homomorphism. It is used in the identification of the Drinfeld basis subtype with the set of roots of the factor $g$ of the $q$-series of the formal group.
